{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prose-intro-q-special-functions","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"prose:intro-q-special-functions","kind":"prose","text":"intro-q-special-functions.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prose:intro-q-special-functions\"></a><p>Three categorical special functions pair with the resolvent: the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-exponential <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\exp_q \\in G(\\mathcal{H}_q)</code>, its primitive inverse <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\log_q</code>, and the level-2 iterated primitive <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Li}_2^q</code>. Each is defined Hopf-algebraically, circumventing analytic representations.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/intro-q-special-functions.md","heading":"","page":"b/prose-intro-q-special-functions","qa":{"counts":{"pass":14,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":5,"unknown":0,"stale":18},"milnor":{"total":1,"notPassing":1}}}
